# P2P protocols (Envy)

## Treat the network as hostile

- Validate sizes, bounds, and types before parsing.
- Reject malformed/oversized packets safely — no crashes, no allocations from untrusted sizes.
- Never trust remote paths/names; prevent traversal and invalid characters.

## Timeouts and responsiveness

- Sockets need sane send/recv timeouts.
- Never block the UI thread on network I/O.
- Handle partial I/O and transient errors (`WSAEWOULDBLOCK`, `WSAEINTR`).

## Rate limiting and caps

- Rate-limit where appropriate (per-peer and/or global).
- Cap memory growth from peer-controlled inputs.

## Compatibility

- Preserve backward compatibility; gate new behavior behind capability detection.
- Unknown fields: ignore safely when possible; never assume fixed layouts.

## Documentation

Protocol behavior changes require updates under `docs/30_protocols/**` in the
same PR when durable wire or compatibility behavior changes.
